 STEP 1 — Add fields to User entity
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Run in terminal:
  php bin/console make:entity User

Add these 3 fields when prompted:
  • email            → string, 180, not null
  • isVerified       → boolean, not null, default: false
  • verificationToken → string, 255, nullable

Then run migrations:
  php bin/console make:migration
  php bin/console doctrine:migrations:migrate

Make sure your User entity has these methods:
  getEmail() / setEmail()
  isVerified() / setIsVerified()
  getVerificationToken() / setVerificationToken()

